221
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:58,320
But be honest.

222
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:02,200
Do you really believe I've developed the sort of personality that makes me feel no shame?

223
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:02,800
Uh...

224
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:04,980
A little bit?

225
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,100
Yes, I do.

226
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:11,620
So, recently, I ran into a buddy of mine from middle school.

227
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:12,960
Go on.

228
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:16,180
Miyamura?

229
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:16,260
Miyamura?

230
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:20,340
Jindo.

231
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:22,900
Damn, man.

232
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:23,720
I'm so jealous.

233
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,940
You're finally growing up on me.

234
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:26,860
Uh...

235
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:27,620
Sorry, what?

236
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:29,040
As if you didn't know.

237
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,060
Oh, I see.

238
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:31,760
Yep, I'm a senior now.

239
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:32,900
You know...

240
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,540
If you weren't held back, you'd be one, too.

241
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:37,840
No!

242
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:39,560
That's not what I meant, you moron!

243
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,200
I was talking about your new girlfriend!

244
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:44,120
I don't have one of those, though.

245
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:45,780
Yeah, like I believe that.

246
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:49,120
It's funny to me, but Hori might not see the humor.

247
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,820
So her name's Hori, huh?

248
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:54,640
You and this girlfriend of yours aren't even on a first-name basis yet?

249
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:59,000
We totally are.

250
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,440
I got caught up in the moment.

251
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,880
Uh-huh.

252
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,880
Sorry, but there it is.

253
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,760
You wanted an example of me getting super flustered, right?

254
00:11:09,140 --> 00:11:10,880
Doesn't get much more flustered than that.

255
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:14,900
Oh, but the next time we talk, I'll set him straight and tell him we aren't really dating.

256
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,380
I don't actually mind if he's not set straight.

257
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,960
The friend in question just texted me.

258
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,320
His ears must have been burning.

259
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:25,280
Let's see.

260
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,440
He said...

261
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,560
Um, you okay?

262
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:31,900
Oh, he's in a picture.

263
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,140
I want to see!

264
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:35,340
Come on!

265
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:36,340
All I want's a peek!

266
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,300
Just give me a second.

267
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:38,160
One.

268
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,160
That was one second.

269
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:40,880
Now hand it over.

270
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:41,700
Idiot thinking.

271
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:43,040
Mia Morda!

272
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,880
Are you even listening to me?

273
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:45,680
Yes, I hear you!

274
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:46,080
Whoa!

275
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,400
Way uncalled for!

276
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:48,660
And delete.

277
00:11:49,820 --> 00:11:51,540
I've never seen this side of you.

278
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:52,840
Is everything okay?

279
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,180
Oh, yeah.

280
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:55,400
Everything's fine.

281
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,000
You know how guys can be.

282
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:58,260
No worries.

283
00:11:58,380 --> 00:11:59,540
What up, what up?

284
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:00,560
Die!

285
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:04,420
He's your middle school friend.

286
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,480
And you say hello by saying die?

287
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,000
That how you always talk?

288
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,640
He really does flip his lid sometimes.

289
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:15,060
Hey, if you want to talk like that with Toru, you should try it.

290
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:18,440
Well, if the two of us become better friends, then maybe.

291
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,300
And he's shy about the weirdest stuff.

292
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,400
The two of you seem like good friends to me.

293
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:23,640
You really think so?

294
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:25,500
Kind of crazy how that happened, huh?

295
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,360
You've reclaimed the creepy crown.

296
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:31,360
There's still so much I don't know about Mia Morda.

297
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:34,120
What kind of kid was he like in middle school?

298
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:35,660
I'm curious.

299
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,060
Okay.

300
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,200
I think I got everything I needed.

301
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:47,860
Oh, crap.

302
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,100
Did I get sick from blasting the AC?

303
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:51,260
No.

304
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:54,120
The only people who catch cold in the summer are morons.

305
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:54,220
Hey, hey, Horty.

306
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:54,800
Huh?

307
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,560
Who's he?

308
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:00,160
What?

309
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:01,460
They have a new single?

310
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,260
Just came out last week.

311
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,600
She was a bro and let me borrow it.

312
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:07,320
Nice.

313
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,660
I might ask him for it.

314
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:11,060
The vocals are totally insane and...

315
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:11,400
Hold up.

316
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,120
The girl getting hit on.

317
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:14,260
Is that Horty?

318
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:14,820
Huh?

319
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:16,020
What are you...

320
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:18,020
Hey, Horty...

321
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:19,860
What the hell are you doing, Shinko?

322
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:20,200
Oh!

323
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:23,360
Hey, punch that dude with zero hesitation.

324
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,080
Ding-a-ling.

325
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:24,980
Stop!

326
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:28,040
I've been your friend for forever, man.

327
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:30,020
You can't even introduce me?

328
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:31,420
Second year, Koichi Shindo.

329
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:32,400
He went to the same school.

330
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:32,960
That satisfactory?

331
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,320
For an online search, it's satisfactory.

332
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,900
Miyamura, do you actually know him?

333
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:39,300
Uh, mm-mm.

334
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,740
You just admitted he went to your school.

335
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,820
Wait, second year?

336
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:44,720
Mm-hmm.

337
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:45,880
I was held back.

338
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:47,480
Which means...

339
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,640
He's as dumb as they come.

340
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,260
Stupid is as Shindo does.

341
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:51,860
Hey, I go to Yasaka, though.

342
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:52,620
So mean.

343
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:53,340
Horty-hai!

344
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:56,880
Still, given the chance, I'd change and go to Katagiri with you.

345
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:57,640
Huh?

346
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:58,500
But why?

347
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:00,980
Because you make it seem like a good time.

348
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:03,480
Or your girl's a good time.

349
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,980
I told you it isn't like that!

350
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:07,820
You're so cute when you're shy.

351
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:08,820
Shut your mouth!

352
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,880
Okay, guys.

353
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:12,100
If we're gonna talk, can we get out of this heat, please?

354
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:12,680
Sure.

355
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,220
Let's go chill out at a restaurant.

356
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,660
Or you can just leave!

357
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:26,160
That bell means we gotta switch classrooms, doesn't it?

358
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:27,420
Better hustle.

359
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:29,760
Yo, Shindo, wait up!

360
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:36,420
Oh, forgot my notebook.

361
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:37,280
Go on ahead!

362
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:42,100
Coming to class?

363
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,220
It starts in two minutes.

364
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:00,060
Sheesh, I mean, at least pick up your stuff.

365
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:02,620
Here you go.

366
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,740
Uh...

367
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:07,840
Yamamura?

368
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:10,600
That's wrong.

369
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:11,260
Huh?

370
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,240
What's wrong?

371
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:14,260
My name isn't Yamamura.

372
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:15,760
I was just kidding!

373
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,240
Everyone knows you're Yamamoto!

374
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:18,880
You're getting even colder!

375
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:20,620
Is Yamakawa warmer?

376
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,800
Yama's not part of it!

377
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:23,400
Kawada!

378
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:26,780
You seriously should have stopped guessing like two names ago.

379
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:30,480
I haven't talked to a classmate or raised my voice in such a long time.

380
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,980
Feels weird to be doing it now.

381
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:34,680
For real?

382
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:35,820
Come on, man.

383
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,480
Yeah, right.

384
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:37,880
Miyamura!

385
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:39,360
Huh?

386
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,200
Hey, that's mine.

387
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,900
I just want to sip this all.

388
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:46,600
You catch the Osaka set on TV?

389
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,520
Talk about a concert!

390
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,080
Yeah, I know!

391
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:51,180
It was so cool!

392
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:53,600
And how awesome were the lights and special effects!

393
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:55,760
Makes me want to go to one in person.

394
00:15:55,760 --> 00:16:02,700
Shindo, you've been hanging with that Miyamura kid a lot lately.

395
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:04,420
I have.

396
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:05,340
Your point is?

397
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,840
My point is that I think you should stop it.

398
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:13,940
He's depressing and gloomy, and all those piercings make him look even weirder.

399
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:19,160
I've seen his type, and when they snap, everybody better duck and cover because shit gets crazy.

400
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:19,940
That's why...

401
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:23,960
Whose fault is it that he's dark and gloomy?

402
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,540
And I know what's really going on.

403
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,740
You're unhappy with him because you think he's stealing me from you.

404
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,600
Don't worry.

405
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,240
We'll hang sometime soon.

406
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,680
My whole middle school experience has changed.

407
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,600
All thanks to Shindo.

408
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:54,040
And the one who's changed my high school experience.

409
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,140
Because you make it seem like a good time.

410
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:59,420
Pick up the pace, huh?

411
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:01,280
It's Hori.

412
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:02,620
Hands down.

413
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:06,100
Whoa!

414
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,360
That's one high fever, sissy!

415
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:10,500
And mom already went to work, too!

416
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:11,620
This is bad!

417
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:14,960
Hang on.

418
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,060
You going somewhere?

419
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,040
School?

420
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:19,280
You can't go to school with a fever that high!

421
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,820
What I can't do is catch a cold when it's still summertime.

422
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,060
Only morons would do something so lame.

423
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:27,440
But you have one!

424
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,880
I gotta go...

425
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,300
Hey!

426
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,580
Give me my bag!

427
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:34,380
The only place you're going is back to bed, sissy!

428
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:36,200
I gotta go to school!

429
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,640
Don't die while I'm gone, okay?

430
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:39,380
I won't die, silly.

431
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:40,540
I promise.

432
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:42,180
I'll hold you to it!

433
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:48,040
I'll see you next time.

434
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:48,720
so fast.

435
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:01,320
Kyoko.

436
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:05,320
I'm sorry, Kyoko.

437
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,460
But there's an emergency at work.

438
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,780
I wish I could stay here and be with you.

439
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:10,900
But I have to go.

440
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,940
Mommy, I thought...

441
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:25,940
I can't breathe out of my nose.

442
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:27,660
Would you like a towel?

443
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,080
Yeah, thank you.

444
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:30,940
No problem.

445
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,220
Let me know when you need a dry one.

446
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,920
And I picked up a sports drink for you, too.

447
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:38,160
Okay.

448
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,800
Are you real?

449
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:40,560
Huh?

450
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:42,160
I'm real.

451
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:45,000
Sota called me saying you were on your deathbed,

452
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:45,960
so I stopped by.

453
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:47,540
Gotcha.

454
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,700
You fully intended to go to school,

455
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:54,660
even with a fever of...

456
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:56,440
38, uh...

457
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:56,660
Hmm?

458
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:58,280
37?

459
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:00,820
Yeah, somewhere around there.

460
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,320
Take any meds?

461
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:05,080
A little while ago.

462
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,140
Okay.

463
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:06,240
Okay.

464
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:07,580
Good.

465
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:14,300
Change out of your uniform before you fall back asleep.

466
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,160
Honey?

467
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:17,000
Hey!

468
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:18,500
What's wrong?

469
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:21,260
Uh...

470
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:23,180
Where are you going?

471
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:24,180
Uh...

472
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:25,700
I was gonna get you some water.

473
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,600
Where are you going?

474
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:28,780
Okay.

475
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:36,680
Listen.

476
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:38,140
For real, though.

477
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,840
You need to lie down.

478
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:42,500
Where are you going?

479
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:44,340
Tell me.

480
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:45,760
Kyoko.

481
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,080
You've always been so good at toughing things out.

482
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,140
I'm sorry I take advantage of that.

483
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,240
Don't be.

484
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,020
Daddy isn't around now.

485
00:19:54,020 --> 00:19:56,000
And works hard enough as it is.

486
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:56,460
Plus,

487
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:58,560
I'm not a little kid anymore.

488
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:00,000
I'll be okay.

489
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,520
Have a good day, Mommy.

490
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:04,600
Why?

491
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:08,240
Why are you never, ever, ever here,

492
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:09,500
even when I need you?

493
00:20:09,940 --> 00:20:11,280
Where are you going?

494
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:17,480
You keep asking where I'm going.

495
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:19,780
That's what you say.

496
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:20,660
But really,

497
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,700
I think you mean,

498
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:24,680
please don't go, right?

499
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,780
Where are you going?

500
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,620
I'm staying right here.

501
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,540
Until you don't need me.

502
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:42,260
Or get sick and tired of looking at me.

503
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,340
Or flat out tell me to buzz off.

504
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:47,200
Or I'll stay wherever you are, Hori.

505
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,460
I'm not going anywhere.

506
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:52,460
Okay.

507
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,620
Can you promise me I'll drink some water later?

508
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:07,780
That's hi.

509
00:21:07,780 --> 00:21:09,600
I called your mom

510
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,560
and then told Ishikawa

511
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,680
to tell school you're sick.

512
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:16,840
Also,

513
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:18,400
I...

514
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,220
I'm in love with you, Hori.

515
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:23,400
Have been for a while.

516
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:26,800
Anyway,

517
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:28,080
there are plenty of drinks

518
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,000
and food in the fridge.

519
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,440
If you need anything,

520
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:33,700
call or text me.

521
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:35,240
I'll come running.

522
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:45,640
Oh my gosh, oh my gosh, oh my gosh.

523
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:46,900
Did he really just say that?

524
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:48,500
He practically shucked the fever

525
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:49,340
out of my system.

526
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:51,180
I'm sick and stuffed up

527
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:52,480
and he chooses now of all days

528
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:53,040
to tell me.

529
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,940
He knew I was awake, right?

530
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,660
I need to know for sure

531
00:21:57,660 --> 00:21:58,960
that wasn't a hallucination.

532
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:02,200
that I don't want to make him say it again.

533
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:07,120
Maybe I'll pretend like I was asleep

534
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,440
and missed what he said.

535
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:10,260
That way,

536
00:22:10,660 --> 00:22:12,580
we can stay as we are

537
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:13,540
for a little longer.

538
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,640
while you have a fertig

539
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,240
and a little longer.

540
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:26,660
So,

541
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:34,660
I've seen my dreams, the night is a beautiful night

542
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:39,660
I'll see you again tomorrow, and I'll see you again

543
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:43,660
I'll see you again, and I'll see you again

544
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:47,660
I'll see you again

545
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:53,660
Long袖のシャツに見覚えある道

546
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:58,660
少し寂しそうに見えた

547
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:05,660
胸が苦しくなるけど暖かい

548
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:12,660
気づいた冬の朝だ

549
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:17,660
約束するよ

550
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:24,660
近くにいるから見えないものほど

551
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:29,660
大事にするよ

552
00:23:29,660 --> 00:23:34,660
言葉にできないんだけどね

553
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:49,660
寂しい

554
00:23:49,660 --> 00:23:51,660
寂しい

555
00:23:51,660 --> 00:23:54,660
寂しい

556
00:23:54,660 --> 00:23:59,660
ローチ

